=================================================================
WHY PAGES 404'd IN PRODUCTION (the real root cause)
=================================================================
The homepage (/) worked but /index.html, /weather.html, and
/database/index.html all 404'd. The files were never missing — this
is the classic signature of a PARTIAL or WRONG-LEVEL upload: only the
content that resolves to "/" made it into the Pages project root, so
everything else had nothing to serve.

Two things made that worse and are now fixed:

1. The zip used to contain a WRAPPER folder (tx-plants-site-v6.5/...).
   If that folder itself got dragged into Cloudflare, every file landed
   one directory too deep and only the root resolved. v7 ships the site
   files at the TOP LEVEL of the zip — there is no wrapper folder to get
   wrong.

2. _redirects had a self-referential rule: /*.html -> /:splat.html 200.
   A rule that maps a path to itself can resolve to a 404 on Pages. It
   was unnecessary anyway — Pages already serves every .html file at its
   clean URL and 308-redirects /page.html -> /page natively. Removed.

